<h3>🔒 Is RedotPay Safe?</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Requires <strong>identity verification (KYC)</strong> for all users.</li>
  <li><strong>Two-factor authentication (2FA)</strong>, biometrics and configurable spending limits.</li>
  <li>Option to <strong>freeze the card</strong> instantly from the app if you lose it.</li>
  <li>Funds are held in custody with <strong>Cactus Custody</strong> in segregated wallets, with <strong>insurance coverage</strong>.</li>
  <li>Complies with the <strong>PCI DSS</strong> card data security standard.</li>
</ul>
<p>⚠️ <strong>Important:</strong> RedotPay is a <strong>custodial</strong> wallet, which means the company holds your cryptocurrencies for you. It's great for spending, but it's not a replacement for a self-custody wallet (where only you hold the private keys) if you want to store large amounts. Use it for what it does best: <strong>paying</strong>.</p>

